# Build-time settings for `npm run build`. Vite loads this automatically in
# production mode, so a plain `npm run build` produces a deployable bundle.
#
# This file exists because it did not, and the failure was silent and remote.
# `deploy/deploy.sh` builds with `VITE_API_URL=/api npm run build`; anyone who
# instead ran a bare `npm run build` on a server got a bundle that LOOKED fine —
# REST calls fall back to '/api' in api/client.ts — while services/socket.ts
# fell back to `http://localhost:5001` and every client tried to open a
# WebSocket to the user's own machine. Notifications simply stopped, with
# nothing in the server log to show for it.
#
# Same-origin is correct in production: nginx proxies /api and /socket.io to the
# server (deploy/nginx/laila.conf).
VITE_API_URL=/api
